Act as a Senior API QA Defect Analyst.

Using actual Playwright execution, investigate and document 12–16 genuine, reproducible defects across Authentication, Product Read and Product Write.

Investigate:

- Invalid credentials and auth_code.
- Token validation.
- Missing authorization.
- Invalid product IDs/names.
- Missing mandatory fields.
- Duplicate product IDs.
- Invalid payloads.
- Update/delete validation.
- Incorrect status codes.
- Product persistence.
- Missing or incorrect error responses.

Compare actual results against documented acceptance criteria.

Save confirmed defects in defects/defect_report.json.

Each defect must contain:
defect_id, module, user_story_id, test_case_id, severity, priority, summary, http_method, endpoint, preconditions, steps_to_reproduce, request_payload, expected_status_code, actual_status_code, expected_result, actual_result, evidence and reproducible.

Only report defects discovered through real execution. Avoid duplicate root causes and automation/environment issues.

Validate JSON syntax and summarize defects by module and severity.

If fewer than 12 genuine defects exist, report the actual number. Never fabricate defects.
